[style name="hell"]
[background arg="res://backrounds/intographics-hell-1690451_1920.jpg" fade="0.0"]
join Urseline (demon/Neutral) center
join Ophelia (Hell  Neutral) right
Urseline (demon/concerned speak): What happened? Are ya alright? Did he say anything to you?
Ophelia (Hell Speak): Nothing! They just said to head to the river Styx and we can leave! Isn't that nice?
Urseline (demon/sad speak): Are you sure that's everything? That doesn't sound right for someone who’s the “Lord of Hell” or whatever.
Ophelia (upset speak): Don’t say that! They might take it back!
Urseline (demon/speak): Take what back?
Ophelia (speaking): We made a deal…
Urseline (demon/concerned): a deal?
Ophelia (Hell Speak): Yep…
Urseline (demon/concerned speak): Fia… You know I can tell when there’s more to it… Baby talk to me…
Ophelia (Hell  Neutral): You’re making this so much harder!
Urseline (demon/sad): What did they make you do…
Ophelia (hopeless): I have to rid my heart of my love for you, Urseline…
Urseline (demon/sad speak): You can’t be serious? We’ll find another way…
Ophelia (Hell Speak): No. I’ve needed to do this for a long time… Urseline.
Urseline (demon/sad speak): Yes?
Ophelia (Hell Speak): Our relationship wasn’t healthy. We were separate people, but we couldn’t do anything without eachother there for us. That isn’t stable. We aren’t stable.
Urseline (demon/speak): What are you saying?
Ophelia (upset speak): Let’s break up. For real this time. I think that's the best for the both of us
Urseline (demon/speak): I can’t believe this! You’d listen to a random person just like that?
Ophelia (upset speak): There are no other options!
Urseline (demon/speak): There’s always other options!
Ophelia (hopeless): Like what?
Urseline (demon/speak): I don't know! You figured out how to get here, didn't you? Why can’t you get out?
Ophelia (Hell Determined Speak): I was meant to bring you back to earth! And I messed that up too….
Urseline (demon/speak): You didn’t mess up… Because you’re here! With me!
Ophelia (upset speak): That's the problem! I don’t want to be here! I want to be at home, and you’re not helping with it!
Urseline (demon/speak): You sound just like you were that night!
Ophelia (hopeless):  …
Narrator: A coin pops out from thin air in front of the two of them, glistening in the reddish hues surrounding them